// A constructor pattern E.B, where the enum E has no constructor B, is a
// compile error (spec/02-syntax.md, Extended match arm patterns).
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The try makes a
// run-time fault print, so an implementation that runs the program fails
// this probe.
enum E { A }
try {
    print match E.A() { case E.B => 1 case _ => 0 };
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}

// STATUS: error
